>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Split`

``` hol4
simpLib.Split : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a split rule for use in one simplifier call.

Passing `Split th` in the theorem list of a `simpLib` simplification
conversion or tactic adds `th` as a split looper for that call, as
`simpLib.add_split th` does. A rule that is not a split rule is ignored
with a warning.

`simpLib.Split` is [`markerLib.Split`](#markerLib.Split).

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss
     [simpLib.Split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)]
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”)
     (Context.snapshot());
```

### See also

[`markerLib.Split`](#markerLib.Split),
[`simpLib.add_split`](#simpLib.add_split),
[`splitLib.SPLIT_TAC`](#splitLib.SPLIT_TAC),
[`simpLib.ExclX`](#simpLib.ExclX).
